{
  "id": "book-19",
  "checkpoint": 3,
  "title": "A Place to Buy a Map",
  "summary": "Na manhã seguinte, Paul volta ao café e pede ajuda para encontrar um lugar onde possa comprar um mapa.",
  "audio_url": "/audios/book-19.mp3",
  "word_count_target": 125,
  "story_en": "The next morning, Paul returns to the café. He sees the same man near the door and walks over to his table.\n\n“Good morning,” Paul says. “How are you today?”\n\n“I’m good,” the man says. “And you?”\n\n“I’m fine. I have a question. Do you know a good place to buy a map?”\n\nThe man closes his book and thinks for a moment. “Yes. There is a small shop near the main street. It opens early, and the people there can help you.”\n\n“Thank you,” Paul says. “Is it far from here?”\n\n“No, it is not far. Walk down this street and turn left at the next corner. You will see the shop near a large window.”\n\nPaul smiles. “That sounds easy.”\n\nThe man smiles too. “Good. Take your time, and ask for help if you need it.”\n\nPaul thanks him and leaves the café. He walks toward the main street, thinking about his next step.",
